# Build products. This list is the Makefile's `clean` target, restated —
# if you add a binary there, add it here, because the two drifting apart is
# how a 500KB test binary ends up in a commit.

# The two shipped binaries (Makefile: all).
satl
satl-term

# The sixteen test binaries (Makefile: TESTBINS), each built in its own folder
# under satellite_system/tests/ as of the 2026-08-24 restructure -- they used to
# sit beside the code they test, and before that in the repo root.
# library_test_tsan is the ThreadSanitizer build and is 27MB, which is the one
# that really hurts.
#
# console_test was the drift this note kept predicting: it was built, it was
# 950KB, and it was NEVER in this list -- it sat untracked in `git status` until
# the move into src/ rewrote these paths. reg_test did the same thing earlier and
# was tracked at b0185ba, 561KB of binary committed.
#
# The Makefile now keeps ONE list, TESTBINS, and `test` and `clean` both read it
# rather than restating it. This file is still a second hand-written copy and so
# is still the half that can drift; kept alphabetical so a missing name is
# visible, which remains the only defence it has.
satellite_system/tests/ast_test/ast_test
satellite_system/tests/bignum_test/bignum_test
satellite_system/tests/console_test/console_test
satellite_system/tests/env_test/env_test
satellite_system/tests/eval_test/eval_test
satellite_system/tests/format_test/format_test
satellite_system/tests/interp_test/interp_test
satellite_system/tests/lexer_test/lexer_test
satellite_system/tests/library_test/library_test
satellite_system/tests/library_test/library_test_tsan
satellite_system/tests/loader_test/loader_test
satellite_system/tests/parser_test/parser_test
satellite_system/tests/random_test/random_test
satellite_system/tests/reg_test/reg_test
satellite_system/tests/satellite_string_test/satellite_string_test
satellite_system/tests/spacesuit_test/spacesuit_test

# pcg_test is a PROTOTYPE and not a Makefile product, so it is deliberately
# outside the list above rather than another name in it. It is built by hand;
# the source is tracked and the binary is not. What it prototyped has landed as
# random.cpp and random_test, and it is kept as the standalone harness the §18
# timing numbers came out of — one that needs no interpreter to run is worth
# keeping around the next time they have to be taken again.
pcg_test/pcg_test

# Objects. *.o.tmp is the interrupted-compile leftover that `clean`'s own
# *.o does not match — see plans/todo.txt item 5.
*.o
*.o.tmp

# Generated by the Makefile, not authored: .libdir-stamp records the prefix
# baked into system.o so a changed prefix forces a rebuild, and the man pages
# are compressed from the dist/*.1 sources, which ARE tracked.
.libdir-stamp
dist/satl.1.gz
dist/satl-term.1.gz

# The gzip rule writes `$@.tmp` and then moves it, so an interrupted `make
# install` leaves this behind. `clean` does not remove it, which makes it the
# one leftover that shows up as untracked.
dist/*.1.gz.tmp

# Benchmark and example harnesses. Their sources are tracked; these are what
# their Makefiles build. example/website/gtk_window is absent from that
# directory's clean target but is still a build product.
example/cxx_compare/compare
example/cxx_compare/bench
example/cxx_compare/hello
example/py_compare/compare
example/py_compare/.python.out
example/py_compare/.satellite.out
example/website/tour
example/website/gtk_window
example/website/cxx.out
example/website/satellite.out

# dpkg-buildpackage staging. The debian/ sources are tracked; everything
# debhelper writes into it at build time is not. The .deb itself lands in the
# PARENT directory and so never appears here.
debian/.debhelper/
debian/satellite/
debian/satellite-term/
debian/files
debian/debhelper-build-stamp
debian/*.substvars
debian/*.debhelper.log

# GIMP working files. The exported PNGs under icon/ are what the build
# installs and are tracked; the layered .xcf they came from is 23MB, which is
# 23MB every clone pays forever. Kept on disk, out of history: `git add -f` can
# always put one in later, and taking a blob back OUT needs a history rewrite.
icon/**/*.xcf

# The download bundle for satellite.foundation: two binaries and the installer,
# rewritten by every build at the project root. Build products, not sources.
enterprise_download/
satellite_rhel.tar.xz

# Build products that had no entry and were sitting untracked in `git status`:
# a stamp the Makefile regenerates from FORCE and `clean` deletes, a tarball
# made by hand at the project root (the Makefile's own bundle is
# satellite_rhel.tar.xz above, which is why this one slipped the list), and the
# two compiled drivers in speed_test/. The .cpp/.asm/.py/.satl sources beside
# them are tracked; only the binaries are not.
.cxxflags-stamp
satl.tar.xz
speed_test/nasm_speed
speed_test/speed_test

# The build_and_install driver's binary. The SOURCE is committed and the binary
# is not, for the same reason satl and satl-term above are not: it is output.
enterprise_satellite_builder
